## Proposed Changes

### Backend Cognition Engine

#### [MODIFY] [backend/app/cognition/engine.py](file:///D:/AI%20ML%20Project/backend/app/cognition/engine.py)
- Implement `find_sentence_boundary(buffer: str) -> int`:
  - Recognizes sentence terminators: `.`, `!`, `?`, `\n\n`.
  - Avoids false splits on abbreviations (`dr`, `mr`, `mrs`, `ms`, `prof`, `sr`, `jr`, `vs`, `etc`, `eg`, `ie`, `approx`, `inc`, `ltd`).
  - Avoids false splits on decimal numbers (e.g. `3.14`, `0.5`).
  - Handles ellipses (`...`).
- Implement `astream_sentences(...) -> AsyncGenerator[Tuple[str, str], None]`:
  - Routes query to the optimal candidate model (Groq, Gemini, Nemotron, Vision).
  - Uses `model.astream(messages)` to stream tokens.
  - Feeds tokens into a rolling buffer and yields `(sentence, model_name)` immediately whenever a boundary is reached.
  - Flushes remaining buffer content upon completion.
  - Updates `conversation_history` with the full combined reply.
  - Respects `self.abort_requested` on every token and yields immediately on interruption.
- Maintain existing `synthesize_speech` and `abort_generation` logic.

---

### Backend WebSocket API

#### [MODIFY] [backend/app/api/websocket.py](file:///D:/AI%20ML%20Project/backend/app/api/websocket.py)
- Upgrade `background_llm_task`:
  - Initialize an `asyncio.Queue` for sentence chunks.
  - **Producer Task**: Asynchronously iterates over `cognition.astream_sentences()` and puts sentences into the queue.
  - **Consumer Worker**: Pulls each sentence from the queue as soon as it is ready, synthesizes audio via `cognition.synthesize_speech(sentence)`, base64-encodes the bytes, and immediately dispatches an `ai_audio_response` WebSocket message with:
    ```python
    {
        "type": "ai_audio_response",
        "payload": {
            "chunk_index": chunk_idx,
            "text": sentence,
            "accumulated_text": full_text_so_far,
            "audio": speech_b64,
            "state": "speaking",
            "model": model_name,
            "is_final": is_final,
            "timestamp": time.time(),
        }
    }
    ```
  - Emits `ai_state: "speaking"` upon first chunk delivery.
  - Emits final marker (`is_final: True`) when all sentences have completed.
  - Abort handling: If an open-palm gesture or interrupt fires, `cognition.abort_requested` triggers immediate termination of the producer and consumer, draining the queue without further synthesis.

